# Phase 18 consumer statistics callback ownership parity

- Recorded: 2026-10-23 21:02:29 UTC
- Workspace: `/Users/bruce.tsai/Projects/trio/rocketmq-classic`
- Starting revision: `8e801833`
- Implemented revision: `b0189bd3`
- Pinned Java source: RocketMQ 5.5.1, `efa1be59d6fc747ad220f036c86030f05f0419f9`
- Scope: identity and behavior of the five `ConsumerStatsManager` `StatsItemSet` schedules

## Finding and change

Pinned Java creates five `StatsItemSet`s and registers six jobs per set. Each
sample and print callback operates on that set's own metric map. Rust had
queued the same 30 jobs and emitted all five metric groups from every print
callback, multiplying output by five; sample callbacks also advanced every
series at once.

Rust schedule tasks now retain a `StatsItemSetKind`. Each sampler advances only
its matching series, and each print callback emits only its matching metric
group. The schedule remains 30 jobs in Java constructor order. Regressions
verify schedule identity, isolated sampling, and exactly one matching log event
per set.

